home equity and other consumer loans, as well as home equity lines of credit; residential mortgage loans; agricultural loans; acquisition and development loans; municipal loans; and installment and other loans. In addition, it provides services as trustee, executor, administrator, guardian, managing agent, custodian, and investment advisor, as well as other fiduciary services under the Orrstown Financial Advisors name; and retail brokerage services through a third-party broker/dealer arrangement. Further, the company offers fiduciary, investment advisory, insurance, and brokerage services. The company was founded in 1919 and is headquartered in Harrisburg, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Adam L. Metz | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $790,864 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 627 people. Revenue per employee of $402K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $112K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Orrstown Financial Services, In is a small-cap financial services business with a $868M market cap on $252M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +26% over the past three years and +17% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +6.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 8% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $70M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 28 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.92\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.7% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 40% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","11 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Peoples Bancorp of North Carolina (NASDAQ:PEBK) & Orrstown Financial Services (NASDAQ:ORRF) Financial Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/peoples-bancorp-of-north-carolina-nasdaqpebk-orrstown-financial-services-nasdaqorrf-financial-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794573861.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(ORRF) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/151/ORRF_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_111226094401_1794537841.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794537841.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Orrstown Financial Services (NASDAQ:ORRF) vs. Chiba Bank (OTCMKTS:CHBAY) Financial Review","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/orrstown-financial-services-nasdaqorrf-vs-chiba-bank-otcmktschbay-financial-review.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794304748.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.943,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Nordea Bank (OTCMKTS:NRDBY) and Orrstown Financial Services (NASDAQ:ORRF) Financial Analysis","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/nordea-bank-otcmktsnrdby-and-orrstown-financial-services-nasdaqorrf-financial-analysis.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794244511.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Critical Survey: AGI (NYSE:AGBK) & Orrstown Fina